// Package report holds the pure parts of `nxy stats`, `nxy trend` and `nxy statusline`: the text
// helpers of the 1.x reports (cache rebuild lines, the 1h TTL verdict, the subagent time table),
// rtk ledger maths (path normalisation, savings per session, daily totals from `rtk gain`),
// the broad-search and filter summaries, and Settings, the view of the merged config with JS
// semantics. The golden files under testdata/golden/report are generated by the 1.x.
//
// Edges not reproduced: a filter.jsonl row whose filtered_chars or est_tokens is a string (JS
// concatenates; here it counts as 0), a null row (JS throws), integer-like engine, skip-reason or
// command_kind values (JS orders those keys first; the tie order of the sorts follows the
// insertion order here), a project path with characters whose case folding differs between Go and
// V8 (win32 only), DailyFromGain over a `daily` that is not an array, ToNumber of arrays and
// objects in Settings thresholds (NaN here), a theme that is not an object.
//
// Edges of the statusline renderer that the golden does not cover: a theme whose role value is not
// a string (JS stringifies it into the style; here the role keeps the preset's style), a truthy
// model id that is not a string and has a price (JS looks the price up by String(id); here the
// cold-cache line shows no price), and a preset named like an Object.prototype key ("constructor", "toString": JS finds
// the inherited member and breaks; here it falls back to classic as an unknown preset does).
package report
